      "question_html": "A student solved \\( 2(x-4)^2 - 8 = 0 \\) and showed this work:<br><br>Step 1: \\( 2(x-4)^2 = 8 \\)<br>Step 2: \\( (x-4)^2 = 4 \\)<br>Step 3: \\( x - 4 = 2 \\)<br>Step 4: \\( x = 6 \\)<br><br>The student got <strong>x = 6 only</strong>. Select the statement that correctly identifies the error.",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "q14",
          "type": "radio",
          "label": "",
          "options": [
            {
              "value": "A",
              "text": "Step 1 is wrong: should move −8 first before working with the squared term"
            },
            {
              "value": "B",
              "text": "Step 2 is wrong: dividing by 2 gives (x−4)² = 2, not 4"
            },
            {
              "value": "C",
              "text": "Step 3 is wrong: taking the square root requires ±, giving x−4 = ±2, so x = 6 OR x = 2"
            },
            {
              "value": "D",
              "text": "No error — x = 6 is the only solution because the equation has one root"
            }
